course: dictionary
lesson: 4085
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «Ruby stops games an hour before bed now, and the giant pickaxe has gone.» Here giant describes the pickaxe, so it means very big. Ask yourself: what is the giant? The answer is a pickaxe, so giant tells you its size.
explain: «Jonathan, a giant tortoise on St Helena, is reported to be around 190 years old.» Here giant is an adjective, because it describes the tortoise. Check by swapping in very large: «a very large tortoise» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: When giant is a noun, it names a person or thing. In stories, a giant is an imaginary person who is enormously big and strong. A giant can also be someone very important, like «a giant of science». Look at the words around giant to decide which meaning fits.
explain: Context is your clue. «Most goods now cross the sea in standard steel boxes on giant ships.» Giant ships are very large ships, and the sentence is about cargo, not monsters. If your first meaning does not fit, try another one.
fact: Giant (adjective) means very, very large, as in «a giant panda» or «giant ships».
fact: In stories and fairy tales, a giant is an imaginary person who is enormously big and strong, like in Jack and the Beanstalk.
fact: Jupiter is called a gas giant because it is a huge planet made mostly of gas.
fact: A giant can also be a person, company or thing that is very important or successful, like «a giant of science».
fact: There is a pysanka museum in Kolomyia in Ukraine shaped like a giant egg, which shows how the word can describe something huge in real life.
exercise: «Ruby stops games an hour before bed now, and the giant pickaxe has gone.» In this sentence, what does giant mean? | A huge imaginary person | *Very big | Very important | Very quiet
exercise: «Most goods now cross the sea in standard steel boxes on giant ships.» What does giant describe? | The sea, which is very calm | The goods, which are very cheap | The boxes, which are very small | *The ships, which are very large
exercise: In a fairy tale, what is a giant? | *An imaginary person who is enormously big and strong | A tall tree in a forest | A very quiet bird | A small pet tortoise
test: In the phrase «gas giant», what does giant mean? | Very small | *Very large | A story monster | A person who is very important
test: «Jonathan, a giant tortoise on St Helena, is reported to be around 190 years old.» What kind of word is giant here? | Verb | Adverb | Noun | *Adjective
exam: Which meaning fits «a giant of science»? | An imaginary huge monster | A very large tortoise | A very small step | *A very important and successful person
